<main class="lux-article-page"><nav class="lux-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="<?php echo esc_url(luxureat_static_url('en', '')); ?>">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="<?php echo esc_url(luxureat_static_url('en/recipe', '')); ?>">Recipes</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Umbrian Trout with Black Truffle</span></nav><article class="lux-recipe-reader lux-recipe-seo-page"><section class="lux-recipe-hero"><figure><img width="612" height="406" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" src="<?php echo esc_url(get_template_directory_uri() . '/assets/media/journal/recipe-truffle-trout.webp'); ?>" alt="Umbrian Trout with Black Truffle"></figure><div class="lux-recipe-intro"><span>Truffle Recipes</span><h1 id="lux-reader-title">Umbrian Trout with Black Truffle</h1><p>A Valnerina tradition from Umbria, pairing gently cooked trout with black truffle and garlic-scented olive oil.</p><dl class="lux-recipe-facts"><div><dt>Time</dt><dd>35 min</dd></div><div><dt>Difficulty</dt><dd>Medium</dd></div><div><dt>Serves</dt><dd>Serves 2</dd></div></dl></div></section><section class="lux-recipe-body"><aside class="lux-recipe-ingredients"><h2>Ingredients</h2><ul><li>2 whole gutted trout, about 300 g each</li><li>30 g black truffle</li><li>30 g extra-virgin olive oil</li><li>1 garlic clove (about 5 g)</li><li>3 g fine salt</li><li>5 g fresh parsley, optional</li></ul></aside><div class="lux-recipe-method"><h2>Method</h2><ol><li>Clean the trout, rinse and dry thoroughly.</li><li>Season the cavities and surfaces lightly with salt.</li><li>Preheat the oven to 190°C, place the trout in a roasting dish and drizzle with a little oil.</li><li>Roast for 15–18 minutes, until just cooked and 63°C at the centre.</li><li>Warm the remaining oil and crushed garlic over low heat without browning.</li><li>Remove the garlic and add 20 g finely grated black truffle.</li><li>Remove the heads and bones while keeping the fillets intact.</li><li>Spoon over the truffle oil.</li><li>Shave over the remaining 10 g truffle, garnish with parsley if desired and serve immediately.</li></ol></div></section><section class="lux-recipe-nutrition"><header><h2>Estimated nutrition per serving</h2></header><dl><div><dt>Energy</dt><dd>About 2,280 kJ / 545 kcal</dd></div><div><dt>Fat</dt><dd>About 35 g</dd></div><div><dt>of which saturates</dt><dd>About 6 g</dd></div><div><dt>Carbohydrate</dt><dd>About 1 g</dd></div><div><dt>of which sugars</dt><dd>Less than 1 g</dd></div><div><dt>Protein</dt><dd>About 63 g</dd></div><div><dt>Fibre</dt><dd>About 0.5 g</dd></div><div><dt>Sodium</dt><dd>About 730 mg</dd></div></dl><p class="lux-recipe-nutrition-note"><strong>Nutrition note</strong>Estimated per serving.</p></section><section class="lux-recipe-details"><div><dt>Reference region</dt><dd>Valnerina, Umbria</dd></div><div><dt>Suggested oil</dt><dd>A gently fruity extra-virgin olive oil.</dd></div><div><dt>Professional tip</dt><dd>Keep the sauce simple and the fish moist; gentle trout carries the truffle without masking it.</dd></div><div><dt>Food safety</dt><dd>Keep raw fish chilled and separate from ready-to-eat food; cook to 63°C and refrigerate leftovers promptly.</dd></div><div><dt>Allergen note</dt><dd>Contains fish.</dd></div><div><dt>Substitutions</dt><dd>Use another delicate freshwater fish, but do not present it as the traditional Valnerina version.</dd></div><div><dt>Related products</dt><dd><a class="lux-recipe-product-link" href="<?php echo esc_url(luxureat_static_url('en/product', '?category=truffle#product-catalogue')); ?>">LuxurEat (露意膳) black truffle and extra-virgin olive oil products</a></dd></div></section></article></main>
